import ZlibF.Math.DeflateOverlayCertificate

/-!
# The memLevel 1 overlay certificate (`lit_bufsize = 128`)

Generated by `tests/goals/overlay-adversarial/certificate/overlay_cert_choice.py --size 128 --w --lean`; do not edit.
The test `certificate/regenerate.sh` regenerates it and compares.

For the lengths `ll`, `dl`, the actual frequencies `fl`, `fd` and the header length `H` of a
dynamic block with at most 127 symbols, `H + E ≤ 999`, from the header row (the region charges of
the scan under the reference code `κ1`, plus the repair excess `Δ`), the choice row, Kraft, the
Fibonacci bound (weight 130), the end of block, the symbol count and the balance. Three cases:
no forced leaf (`certificate_none`); forced leaves only in the distance tree, which then has two
nonzero lengths (`certificate_dist`); forced leaves in the literal/length tree, which then has two
nonzero lengths (`certificate_lit`). Each class of entries is a sixteen-case `omega` check.

Here the repair excess grows with the number `W` of bit-length symbols: the header row is
`2·(H − 71 − Δ) ≤ Σ charges`, where the charges also pay one bit per bit-length symbol, so a
header bound `H ≤ 71 + Δ + W/2 + refHeaderCost` enters with this `Δ`.
-/

